{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0030","billNumberShort":"H.B. 30","billNumberLong":"HB0030S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0621","shortTitle":"Wildlife Management Area Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"SHALLD","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shallenberger, David","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses wildlife management areas.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>creates the Wildlife Management Area Stewardship Fund;<hr><ltbullet>repeals language related to access to wildlife management areas requiring a hunting, fishing, or combination license;<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>requires that an individual meet certain conditions to access a wildlife management area;<hr><ltbullet>directs the Division of Wildlife Resources (division) to approve an educational video and provide digital verification of completion of the educational video;<hr><ltbullet>provides for exceptions to the conditions to access a wildlife management area;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes rulemaking and requires reporting regarding rulemaking;<hr><ltbullet>provides for voluntary financial contributions for the benefit of wildlife management areas;<hr><ltbullet>permits the division to oversee the provision of volunteer labor to benefit a wildlife management area, including addressing liability issues; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Patricia Owen","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"UXLYMWHJOG","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0030","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2025-10-30 16:28:39.883","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceV